<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gerbod the Fleming</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1070s</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gerbod the Fleming was a Flemish nobleman who received the earldom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chester">Chester</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William the Conqueror</a> around 1070, after the suppression of English resistance in the north and west. He soon returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>, where he was captured in the fighting of 1071, and the earldom was given instead to Hugh d'<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avranches">Avranches</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gerbod-the-fleming.jpg" alt="Gerbod the Fleming" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Romainberth · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ruines_saint_bertin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
